<%# locals: (task: nil, peek: nil) %>
<%# The side panel: runeui's (ui :side_panel), its state this page's own address with ?task=42 (the
    task, tasks/_panel) or ?peek=Client:3 (a client, piece of work or contact, <type>/_peek). The
    layout draws it open from the first paint when the address has one; opening, following (j / k)
    and closing load just its frame, which ApplicationController#render_side_panel answers with
    layouts/shared/side_panel_frame, skipping the page's own action. The side-panel controller on
    <body> adds the links, j / k, prefetching and closing on a click outside. Its contents draw
    their own ✕ (closable: false). %>
<%= ui :side_panel, params: %w[task peek], src: (request.fullpath if task || peek), closable: false, initial_focus: "none", label: (task ? task.title : (peek ? peek_title(peek) : "Details")) do %>
  <%= render "layouts/shared/side_panel_content", task: task, peek: peek %>
<% end %>
